# Attribution correction for AI-authored identities.
#
# Scope, stated honestly: .mailmap remaps **author and committer** names and
# emails. It cannot rewrite commit-message bodies, so it does NOT touch the
# `Co-authored-by:` trailer that two commits (v0.11.3, v0.11.4, April 2026) carry.
# gitmailmap(5) is the authority here; the trailer is body text.
#
# It is kept because it is the right guard for the thing it can fix: if any tool
# ever records an AI identity in the author or committer field, git and GitHub
# will attribute it to the repository owner instead of listing a second name.
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>
Nicholas Glazer <glazer.nicholas@gmail.com> <noreply@anthropic.com>
Nicholas Glazer <glazer.nicholas@gmail.com> Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
